🟢 1. Outbox Pattern (Fintech-grade Implementation)
❌ Problem

You must update DB and publish event:

DB write succeeds ✅

Kafka publish fails ❌ → data inconsistency (critical in fintech)

✅ Core Idea

Write everything in one DB transaction, then publish asynchronously.

🔹 DB Design
orders
------
id | user_id | amount | status

outbox_events
--------------
id | event_type | payload | status | created_at
🔹 Step-by-step Flow
1. Application Transaction
@Transactional
public void createOrder(Order order) {
    orderRepository.save(order);

    OutboxEvent event = new OutboxEvent(
        "OrderCreated",
        toJson(order),
        "NEW"
    );

    outboxRepository.save(event);
}

👉 DB + outbox write = atomic

2. Outbox Publisher (Background Worker)

Options:

Polling (simple)

CDC using Debezium (preferred in fintech)

@Scheduled(fixedDelay = 1000)
public void publishEvents() {
    List<OutboxEvent> events = outboxRepo.findByStatus("NEW");

    for (OutboxEvent e : events) {
        kafkaProducer.send("orders", e.getPayload());
        e.setStatus("SENT");
        outboxRepo.save(e);
    }
}
🔹 Fintech Best Practices

Use CDC (Debezium) instead of polling

Make publisher idempotent

Add event_id (UUID) for deduplication

Monitor lag in outbox table

🔥 Why fintech uses this

Guarantees no lost transactions

Works even during crashes

Audit-friendly (important for compliance)

🟡 2. Kafka Retry + DLQ Implementation
❌ Problem

Consumer fails → message stuck or lost

✅ Pattern

Use:

Retry topics

Dead Letter Queue (DLQ)

🔹 Topic Design
orders.main
orders.retry.1
orders.retry.2
orders.dlq
🔹 Flow

Consume from orders.main

If fails:

Send to retry topic with delay

After max retries:

Send to DLQ

🔹 Example (Spring Kafka style)
@KafkaListener(topics = "orders.main")
public void consume(OrderEvent event) {
    try {
        process(event);
    } catch (Exception e) {
        throw e; // handled by retry config
    }
}
Retry + DLQ Config
@Bean
public DefaultErrorHandler errorHandler(KafkaTemplate template) {
    return new DefaultErrorHandler(
        new DeadLetterPublishingRecoverer(template),
        new ExponentialBackOff(1000, 2.0)
    );
}
🔹 DLQ Message Example
{
  "event": {...},
  "error": "DB timeout",
  "retry_count": 3
}
🔹 Best Practices

Never retry forever ❌

Add retry count header

Alert on DLQ growth

Provide replay tool

🔴 3. Exactly-Once Processing (Advanced)
❌ Problem

Avoid:

Duplicate processing

Data inconsistency

✅ Kafka Exactly-Once Semantics (EOS)
🔹 Key Concepts

Idempotent Producer

Transactional Producer

Transactional Consumer (read-process-write)

🔹 Producer Config
enable.idempotence=true
acks=all
retries=MAX_INT
🔹 Transactional Processing
producer.initTransactions();

try {
    producer.beginTransaction();

    ConsumerRecords records = consumer.poll();

    for (record : records) {
        process(record);
        producer.send(newRecord);
    }

    producer.sendOffsetsToTransaction(offsets, groupId);

    producer.commitTransaction();

} catch (Exception e) {
    producer.abortTransaction();
}
🔹 What this guarantees

Messages processed once and only once

Offsets committed only if processing succeeds

⚠️ Real-world caveat

Kafka guarantees exactly-once only within Kafka.

👉 For DB:
You MUST combine with:

Idempotent writes

OR Outbox pattern

